  "reached_closure_reasoning": {
    "current_delta": "Since managed guards the only changed WF functions are _hook_action and _hook_transition, with one added _hook_review_frontier. Core request-only role paths call none of these. The lazy PR module import exists only inside the new frontier helper, which returns before import unless proof has publication_id. Module initialization adds function definitions only.",
    "historical_scope": "Three request-only contexts and eight recorded state observations remain in research. No task_ids, pending_ids, run_id or clarification session exists in these contexts; no HC is created or admitted.",
    "role_envelopes": "DG and DO bytes, role routing, sealed question/input construction, predecessor evidence, mode/grant acceptance and no-progress policy remain byte-identical to original capture sources. Reached WF adapters and CLI routing are unchanged from managed baseline; own-source loader now verifies current operation inventory, so a valid newly activated current bundle is a required condition.",
    "store": "Store.__init__, lock, commit and owned loader are AST-identical to reviewed managed-guard baseline. Actual lock initializes _hook_active_admissions=[] and writer flags; unchanged request-only decision guard/action and DO paths cannot register hook admissions. Commit admission loop stays empty; navigation-only followup flag stays false for decision writes. Added invocation CAS inventory is read-only and creates no HC/Future. The previous explicit transaction-body normalization argument remains at the historical analysis reference, not replaced by a whole-function equality claim to1f.",
    "strict_boundary": "Historical WF hash differs from current. The unchanged strict current-source core validator must reject the original historical report/capture as a fresh current-native report. No snapshot/profile/role/accounting field is rewritten."
  },
  "required_conditions": [
    "Pass fresh selected core127 unit, standalone, parent-adapter and oracle checks on the final116 source footprint; no earlier Green substitutes.",
    "Pass current116 and invocation/owned-loader deterministic contracts on the exact frozen source; these are separate from historical actor quality and native qualification.",
    "Finish authorized116 commit and owned installer refresh, validate actual operation ownership/current inventory and re-admission.",
    "Let the explicit controller select the completed core127 dependency and its revalidation contract before any acceptance record.",
    "If a changed reachable role or envelope behavior is discovered, or current-native acceptance is explicitly required, use a separately authorized finite actual run instead of this static proposal."
  ],
